🤖 AI CRM Assistant – Project 3

An intelligent AI-powered CRM Assistant that integrates with internal CRM APIs to manage tickets, customers, and conversations using LLM-based tool calling.

This project combines:

🧠 LLM-based AI Agent
⚡ FastAPI Backend
🎨 Streamlit Frontend
🔗 CRM API Integration
🕒Timezone-aware Date Filtering


🚀 Features Implemented

✅ 1. AI Agent with Tool Calling

    Uses LLM to interpret user queries
    Dynamically calls backend tools like:
    fetch_tickets
    Customer sync APIs
    Structured system prompt with strict rules
    Calendar-aware ticket filtering

✅ 2. Ticket Management

Fetch tickets from CRM API

Limit response to first 15 tickets
Return summary:
Total tickets
Open tickets
Closed tickets
Displayed tickets
Strict calendar filtering:

Today

Yesterday

This week

This month

Timezone-aware date comparison

✅ 3. Date Handling (Production-Safe)

Converts created_at string format:

"Tue, 10 Feb 2026"

into Python datetime object

Uses zoneinfo for timezone awareness

Avoids string-based date comparison

Injects dynamic current date into system prompt


✅ 4. Streamlit Frontend

Chat-style UI using st.chat_message

Session state handling

Spinner during API calls

Clean assistant interface

Persistent conversation support

"New Chat" capability (if enabled)

✅ 5. Authentication Flow

Backend login API integration

Token-based request handling

Secure API communication

✅ 6. CRM Sync Integration

Create customer

Sync customer with CRM (HubSpot-style API)

Handle:

409 conflict (already exists)

422 validation errors

Async HTTP calls using httpx

🏗 Architecture
Frontend (Streamlit)
        ↓
FastAPI Backend (AI Agent + Tools)
        ↓
CRM APIs / Database
        ↓
PostgreSQL / MySQL (Conversations + Messages)

🛠 Tech Stack
Layer	Technology
Frontend	Streamlit
Backend	FastAPI
AI Layer	LLM Agent (Tool Calling)
Database	PostgreSQL / MySQL
HTTP Client	httpx
Date Handling	datetime + zoneinfo
ORM	SQLAlchemy
🧠 AI Behavior Rules

The assistant:

MUST call fetch_tickets tool before answering ticket queries

MUST parse created_at into datetime

MUST use timezone-aware current date

MUST apply strict calendar filtering

MUST limit ticket output to first 15 results

MUST return structured summaries

